# Pearl — the reef's one carried treasure.
#
# The simplest model in the set and the one with the least room to be clever: a
# pearl is a sphere, and any silhouette that is not a sphere is not a pearl.
# Everything interesting has to happen in the colour, and there are two things
# to say with it.
#
# **Nacre is not white.** A pearl reads as *lustre* — a pale body with a warm
# shadow side and a cool bloom where the light lands. Modelled as one flat
# white the thing is a golf ball, and at toolbar size a golf ball is a full
# stop. So the sphere carries three bands up its height (`Shade` low, `Nacre`
# through the middle, `Bloom` at the crown) and a single `material_arc` stripe
# of `Sheen` running down one side, which is the specular streak a round
# reflective object has and a flat-shaded low-poly one otherwise cannot.
#
# **The stripe is a whole facet wide.** Twelve sides, so 30° — an arc narrower
# than a facet snaps to that facet's edges and lands as a blotch instead of a
# stripe. That is the same rule `coral_brain.wam` and `sea_shell.wam` are built
# on, and it is the only real constraint on the arcs in this file.
#
# Slightly taller than it is wide, on purpose: `render/ItemModels.js` normalises
# every model by its **Y** extent, so a model that is fattest across the
# equator arrives in the fist and the icon grid a touch larger than its
# neighbours. Half a percent of ovoid costs nothing and keeps it in the family.

model pearl
  height 0.13
  style smooth

palette
  Nacre #ecebe4
  Bloom #ffffff
  Sheen #d8e6f2
  Shade #c3bfb2

skeleton
  # Lifted off y=0 by the amount the start cap bulges below its own first ring.
  # A `dome` cap is a hemisphere on the *outside* of the ring it closes, so a
  # sphere authored from y=0 hangs a thirtieth of itself through the floor —
  # which the lint reports and which matters here for one reason: `Drops` lays a
  # dropped item on the ground, and a pearl embedded in the sand is a pearl you
  # cannot see.
  root air at 0.04
  bone core parent=air dir=up len=0.96

parts
  loft bead bones=air..core material=Nacre sides=12
    ring 0.00 w=0.20 d=0.20 material=Shade
    ring 0.06 w=0.44 d=0.44
    ring 0.14 w=0.64 d=0.64
    ring 0.30 w=0.86 d=0.86 material=Nacre material_arc=Sheen:60-90
    ring 0.52 w=0.94 d=0.94 material_arc=Sheen:60-90
    ring 0.74 w=0.84 d=0.84 material_arc=Sheen:60-90
    ring 0.88 w=0.66 d=0.66 material=Bloom
    ring 0.96 w=0.42 d=0.42
    ring 1.00 w=0.20 d=0.20
    cap start=dome end=dome

checks
  # Round. Both ways, because a pearl that has drifted into an egg or a lozenge
  # in either axis has stopped being one.
  assert width / depth == 1.0 +- 0.02
  assert height / width in 1.0..1.2
  # The lustre survives a ring edit — all four materials have to reach the mesh
  # or this is a white ball again.
  assert materials == 4
  assert parts == 1
  assert tris < 260
  assert bottom(bead) > -0.01
  measure roundness height / width
